## Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+ 
- Next.js 15+
- Tailwind CSS 3.4+
- TypeScript

### Project Structure

Our components are organized in atomic design principles:

- **Foundations/**: Core design tokens (Logo, Colors, etc.)
- **Controls/**: Form controls and input elements  
- **Components/**: Complex reusable components
- **Elements/**: Basic UI building blocks
- **Global/**: App-wide layout components

## Component Usage Patterns

### 1. Import Components

```typescript
// Main components
import { AwardCard } from '@/components/Components/AwardCard'
import { GameCard } from '@/components/Components/GameCard'
import { SearchandFilters } from '@/components/Components/SearchandFilters'

// Controls
import { SearchInput } from '@/components/Controls/SearchInput'
import { FilterButton } from '@/components/Controls/FilterButton'
import { ToggleGroup } from '@/components/Controls/ToggleGroup'

// Elements
import { RatingPopup } from '@/components/Elements/RatingPopup'
```

### 2. Basic Component Usage

#### SearchInput Example
```typescript
<SearchInput
  value={searchQuery}
  onChange={setSearchQuery}
  placeholder="Search games..."
  onClear={() => setSearchQuery('')}
  className="w-full"
/>
```

#### GameCard Example
```typescript
<GameCard
  game={game}
  viewMode="grid"
  variant="balanced"
  onMembershipChange={(gameId, change) => handleMembershipChange(gameId, change)}
/>
```

### 3. Rating System

Use our standardized 1-10 rating system:

- **1**: red-600 (Awful)
- **2**: orange-600 (Bad)  
- **3**: amber-600 (Poor)
- **4**: yellow-600 (Below Average)
- **5**: lime-600 (Average)
- **6**: green-600 (Above Average)
- **7**: emerald-600 (Good)
- **8**: teal-600 (Very Good)
- **9**: cyan-600 (Great)
- **10**: sky-600 (Masterpiece)

## Design System Usage

### Responsive Design

All components follow mobile-first responsive design:

```typescript
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  <GameCard game={game} viewMode="grid" />
</div>
```

### Dark Mode Support

Components support dark mode through Tailwind's dark variant:

```typescript
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
  {/* Component content */}
</div>
```

## Common Patterns

### 1. Loading States
```typescript
{isLoading ? (
  <div className="animate-pulse bg-gray-200 rounded-lg h-48" />
) : (
  <GameCard game={game} />
)}
```

### 2. Empty States
```typescript
{games.length === 0 ? (
  <div className="text-gray-500 text-center py-12">
    <CubeIcon className="w-12 h-12 mx-auto mb-4" />
    <p>No games found matching your criteria.</p>
  </div>
) : (
  <GameList games={games} />
)}
```

## Accessibility Guidelines

All components support:
- Semantic HTML structure
- ARIA labels and descriptions  
- Keyboard navigation
- Focus management
- Screen reader compatibility

